--- Technical ---
### Changed

- Integrate the complete M9 frontend redesign into `main` and include the v1.9.0 release notes. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown, keeping unanchored citations in the sources list through `AssistantMarkdown.Render(markdown, citations)`. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Add a ticket-header primary control that executes the first actionable `SuggestedNextSteps` entry, with remaining steps in an overflow menu. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operated command palette to every page, with navigation from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Update ticket status optimistically in `TicketBoardFeatureState.MoveAsync`, reconciling successful changes and restoring the prior state when a move is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace `AssignTicketDialog.razor` and `ChangeStatusDialog.razor` with inline header popovers for assignee and status changes. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges by matching citation titles in assistant answers, retaining the numbered sources list for citations that are not anchored. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Include the active agent roster in each chat system prompt so the assistant can identify valid assignees without first calling `assign_ticket`. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Require `AgentLoop` to invoke `check_grounding` through `tool_choice` once after retrieval supplies passages and before answer tokens stream. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Use `Theme/DesignTokens.cs` as the shared source for the app's palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Wrap `.board-card__title` in a grid-item container so long titles clamp to two lines with an ellipsis. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Apply assistant panel styles through `::deep .assistant-chat` so the composer layout keeps the send button inside the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Give the `Category` column a 140px width and render its header in uppercase to prevent overlap with `Due`. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Set a chat system-prompt policy that requires successful tool results before claiming a change and avoids confirmation when the user has already requested it. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert ticket-summary timestamps to `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Report non-transient `search_knowledge_base` failures with `IsError: true`, while preserving the unavailable result as non-error. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Use `SemanticGroundingEvaluator` to score answer sentences against retrieved passages by cosine similarity, falling back to `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` when embeddings are unavailable or fail. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
